# WIV MCP workflow guidance

When the user asks about data in their Wiv organization, use the tools and resources provided by the `wiv-api` server.

- Resolve names with list/search tools instead of guessing IDs.
- Read the step catalog and workflow authoring guide before creating or replacing workflows.
- Read the widget catalog and dashboard authoring guide before writing dashboard layouts.
- Retrieve the current object before a full update and preserve fields outside the requested change.
- Confirm destructive actions before calling delete, stop, or full-replacement tools.
- Use metadata patch tools when the user is only changing names, descriptions, or labels.
- For MSP customer writes, reconnect as that customer organization instead of attempting an impersonated write.
